   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# God Rays\n\nVolumetric light rays fan out from a source just above the frame: soft, slowly moving shafts of light in your palette, drawn in WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A hero or reveal scene wants cinematic volumetric light rays from a corner source.\n- You want atmosphere and depth behind a title without geometric structure.\n- The palette is dark and you want soft neutral rays (override `colors` to brand-tint).\n\nAvoid when:\n- The brief bans decorative glow: keep `bloom` and `intensity` restrained so it does not read as a generic glow.\n- You want structured or cellular motion: use shader-dot-orbit or shader-voronoi.\n- Bright rays would wash out foreground text: lower `intensity` and `bloom`.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- colors (string): Ray colors, default \"#5a5a7e, #8a8a95, #ffffff, #3a3a5c\"\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#12121a\"\n- color_bloom (color): Bloom color, default \"#3a3a5c\"\n- intensity (number, 0-2): Intensity, default 0.8\n- density (number, 0-1): Density, default 0.3\n- spotty (number, 0-1): Spotty, default 0.3\n- bloom (number, 0-1): Bloom, default 0.4\n- mid_size (number, 0-1): Glow size, default 0.2\n- mid_intensity (number, 0-1): Glow intensity, default 0.4\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
